<!--
  Interactive Warehouse Benchmark — HTML report template.

  This file is the authoritative layout and copy for benchmark reports produced
  by the `interactive-benchmark` skill. Do NOT change the structure or CSS when
  filling it in — only replace the {{PLACEHOLDER}} tokens with real values.

  =============================================================================
  Placeholder reference
  =============================================================================

  Header / summary
    {{SOLUTION_NAME}}           Solution name (SOLUTION_NAME from .env).
    {{DATASET_LABEL}}           Human-readable dataset label (e.g. "TPCH SF100").
    {{RUN_DATE}}                YYYY-MM-DD of the run.
    {{USER_COUNT}}              Concurrent users (e.g. 50).
    {{RUN_TIME}}                Locust run duration text (e.g. "3-minute run").

  Executive summary tiles
    {{P95_INT_SERVER_MS}}       Interactive server-side P95 (ms).
    {{P95_INT_SERVER_STATUS}}   "under goal" | "above goal" (tile pill).
    {{P95_INT_SERVER_CLASS}}    Pill class: "ok" | "warn" | "bad".
    {{P95_STD_SERVER}}          Standard server-side P95, formatted (e.g. "18.7 s").
    {{P95_SPEEDUP}}             Server-side P95 speedup vs standard (e.g. "15.1×").
    {{P50_INT_SERVER_MS}}       Interactive server-side P50 (ms).
    {{P50_INT_SERVER_CLASS}}    Pill class for P50 server tile.
    {{P50_INT_SERVER_STATUS}}   Pill copy for P50 server tile.
    {{P50_INT_CLIENT_MS}}       Interactive client-side P50 (ms).
    {{P50_INT_CLIENT_CLASS}}    Pill class for P50 client tile.
    {{P50_INT_CLIENT_STATUS}}   Pill copy for P50 client tile.
    {{TOTAL_REQUESTS}}          Total Locust request count (int + std).
    {{TOTAL_FAILURES}}          Failure count.
    {{FAILURE_CLASS}}           Pill class for failure tile.
    {{FAILURE_STATUS}}          Pill copy for failure tile (e.g. "100% success").
    {{VERDICT_PARAGRAPH}}       1-2 sentence overall verdict.

  Benchmark setup
    {{CONNECTION}}              Snowflake connection name.
    {{DB_STD}}                  Fully-qualified standard schema (DB.SCHEMA).
    {{DB_INT}}                  Fully-qualified interactive schema (DB.SCHEMA).
    {{STD_WH}}                  Standard warehouse name.
    {{STD_WH_DESC}}             "X-Small · Gen2" or equivalent size/gen text.
    {{INT_WH}}                  Interactive warehouse name.
    {{INT_WH_DESC}}             Interactive WH descriptor incl. size, MIN/MAX
                                clusters, scaling policy, and fallback WH.
    {{SPAWN_RATE}}              Locust spawn rate (e.g. 5).
    {{RUN_TIME_SEC}}            Run time in seconds (e.g. 180).
    {{LOCUST_VERSION}}          Locust version reported by the container.
    {{API_WORKERS}}             API uvicorn worker count.
    {{API_POOL_SIZE}}           API POOL_SIZE.
    {{API_INSTANCE_FAMILY}}     SPCS instance family (e.g. CPU_X64_M).
    {{API_INSTANCE_COUNT}}      API service instance count.

  Query and variants
    {{PRIMARY_QUERY}}           The base SQL query (inside <pre>).
    {{VARIANT_ROWS}}            HTML <tr>… rows describing each SQL variant.

  Table details
    {{TABLE_DETAIL_ROWS}}       HTML <tr>… rows for each source table.
    {{WORKING_SET_GB}}          Total working-set size in GB (formatted, e.g. "4.4").
    {{WORKING_SET_NOTE}}        Free-text note on cache fit and pruning behavior.

  Client-side results
    {{CLIENT_INTERACTIVE_ROW}}  <tr> for /api/run/interactive (Req#, req/s, Min,
                                P50, P90, P95, P99, Max — all ms).
    {{CLIENT_STANDARD_ROW}}     <tr> for /api/run/standard.

  Server-side results
    {{SERVER_INTERACTIVE_ROW}}  <tr> for interactive WH (N, P50, P90, P95, P99,
                                avg compile, avg exec, avg queue, avg MB scan).
    {{SERVER_STANDARD_ROW}}     <tr> for standard WH.
    {{SERVER_N_NOTE}}           Note explaining N discrepancy (fallback story),
                                or "" if standard N == locust standard hits.

  Bottleneck diagnosis
    {{DELTA_TABLE_ROWS}}        <tr>… for P50/P95/P99 with Locust, Snowflake,
                                and delta values for both warehouses.
    {{STANDARD_DELTA_ANALYSIS}} 1-paragraph interpretation of standard delta.
    {{INTERACTIVE_DELTA_ANALYSIS}} 1-paragraph interpretation of interactive
                                delta pattern (constant/growing).
    {{BOTTLENECK_VERDICT_CLASS}} "good" | "note" | "bad-box".
    {{BOTTLENECK_VERDICT}}      Explicit conclusion naming which layer to
                                optimize (Snowflake vs API vs fallback).

  Percentile bars
    {{BAR_CLIENT_ROWS}}         6 <div class="bar-row">… entries for client-side
                                P50/P95/P99 int and std.
    {{BAR_SERVER_ROWS}}         6 rows for server-side percentiles.

  Query profile health
    {{PROFILE_TOP_ROWS}}        <tr>… for top ~10 slowest interactive queries.
    {{PROFILE_VERDICT_LIST}}    <li>… items summarizing compile/queue/scan tail.

  Escalation path (populated from Step 13c)
    {{ITERATION_HISTORY}}       HTML fragment (a small table or <ul>) showing
                                each benchmark iteration that led to the final
                                numbers: starting warehouse size,
                                MAX_CLUSTER_COUNT, server-side P95, and the
                                decision taken (met goal / scale up / scale out
                                / limit-bound). If only one iteration was
                                needed, emit a single-row table with decision
                                "goal met at initial configuration" — do NOT
                                emit an empty string, the section must always
                                have content.

  Recommendations
    {{RECOMMENDATIONS_TO_MEET_GOAL}}   <ol><li>…</li></ol> of actionable steps
                                        to hit the latency goal.
    {{RECOMMENDATIONS_ALREADY_OK}}     <ul><li>…</li></ul> of "keep as-is" items.
    {{RECOMMENDATIONS_GENERAL}}        <ul><li>…</li></ul> of general guidance.

  Configuration
    {{CONFIG_COMPUTE_POOLS}}    <ul><li>…</li></ul> describing compute pools.
    {{CONFIG_API}}              <ul><li>…</li></ul> describing API server.
    {{CONFIG_INT_WH}}           <ul><li>…</li></ul> describing interactive WH.
    {{CONFIG_LOCUST}}           <ul><li>…</li></ul> describing Locust settings.

  =============================================================================
  Sizing the horizontal-bar comparison
  =============================================================================
  The bar-row widths are relative percentages within their section. Pick a
  common scale-max (the slowest value in the section) and compute each bar
  width as round(value / scale_max * 100). Keep the same scale-max for both
  interactive and standard bars in the same section so the visual ratio is
  faithful.

  =============================================================================
-->
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Interactive Warehouse Benchmark — {{SOLUTION_NAME}} — {{RUN_DATE}} ({{USER_COUNT}} users)</title>
<style>
  :root { --snow-blue:#29B5E8; --snow-navy:#11567F; --ok:#1a9c5b; --warn:#c98600; --bad:#c74141; --bg:#f7fbfd; --fg:#1d2939; --muted:#5b6b7a; --card:#ffffff; --border:#e3ebf1; }
  * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  body { font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"SF Pro Text","Segoe UI",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; margin:0; padding:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--fg); line-height:1.5; }
  header { background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--snow-navy),var(--snow-blue)); color:white; padding:28px 40px; }
  header h1 { margin:0 0 4px; font-size:24px; font-weight:600; }
  header .sub { opacity:.9; font-size:14px; }
  main { max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:28px 40px 80px; }
  section { background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; padding:22px 26px; margin-bottom:20px; }
  section h2 { margin:0 0 14px; font-size:18px; color:var(--snow-navy); border-bottom:2px solid var(--snow-blue); padding-bottom:8px; }
  section h3 { font-size:15px; color:var(--snow-navy); margin:18px 0 8px; }
  table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:14px; }
  th,td { text-align:left; padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); }
  th { background:#eef7fb; color:var(--snow-navy); font-weight:600; }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom:none; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align:right; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; font-family:"SF Mono",Menlo,monospace; }
  code, pre { font-family:"SF Mono",Menlo,Consolas,monospace; font-size:13px; }
  pre { background:#0f172a; color:#e2e8f0; padding:14px 16px; border-radius:6px; overflow-x:auto; }
  .kv { display:grid; grid-template-columns:220px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; font-size:14px; }
  .kv dt { color:var(--muted); }
  .kv dd { margin:0; font-family:"SF Mono",Menlo,monospace; }
  .pill { display:inline-block; padding:2px 10px; border-radius:12px; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; }
  .ok { background:#e2f5ec; color:var(--ok); }
  .warn { background:#fbf1d9; color:var(--warn); }
  .bad { background:#fbe1e1; color:var(--bad); }
  .grid2 { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:16px; }
  .grid3 { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:16px; }
  .metric { padding:14px; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; background:#f9fcfe; }
  .metric .lbl { font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.5px; }
  .metric .val { font-size:28px; font-weight:600; color:var(--snow-navy); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .bar { height:22px; background:var(--snow-blue); border-radius:4px; }
  .bar.std { background:#c74141; }
  .bar-row { display:grid; grid-template-columns:70px 1fr 110px; align-items:center; gap:12px; margin:6px 0; font-size:13px; }
  .bar-row .lbl { color:var(--muted); font-family:"SF Mono",Menlo,monospace; }
  .bar-row .val { text-align:right; font-family:"SF Mono",Menlo,monospace; font-weight:600; }
  ul { margin:0; padding-left:22px; }
  li { margin:4px 0; }
  .note { background:#fbf1d9; border-left:4px solid var(--warn); padding:10px 14px; border-radius:4px; font-size:13px; margin:12px 0; }
  .good { background:#e2f5ec; border-left:4px solid var(--ok); padding:10px 14px; border-radius:4px; font-size:13px; margin:12px 0; }
  .bad-box { background:#fbe1e1; border-left:4px solid var(--bad); padding:10px 14px; border-radius:4px; font-size:13px; margin:12px 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <h1>Interactive Warehouse Benchmark</h1>
  <div class="sub">Solution: <strong>{{SOLUTION_NAME}}</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{DATASET_LABEL}} &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{RUN_DATE}} &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{USER_COUNT}} concurrent users &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{RUN_TIME}}</div>
</header>

<main>

<section>
  <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
  <div class="grid3">
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="lbl">P95 — Snowflake (interactive)</div>
      <div class="val">{{P95_INT_SERVER_MS}} ms <span class="pill {{P95_INT_SERVER_CLASS}}">{{P95_INT_SERVER_STATUS}}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="lbl">P95 — Snowflake (standard)</div>
      <div class="val">{{P95_STD_SERVER}} <span class="pill bad">saturated</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="lbl">P95 speedup — server-side</div>
      <div class="val">{{P95_SPEEDUP}}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="lbl">P50 — Snowflake (interactive)</div>
      <div class="val">{{P50_INT_SERVER_MS}} ms <span class="pill {{P50_INT_SERVER_CLASS}}">{{P50_INT_SERVER_STATUS}}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="lbl">P50 — Client (interactive)</div>
      <div class="val">{{P50_INT_CLIENT_MS}} ms <span class="pill {{P50_INT_CLIENT_CLASS}}">{{P50_INT_CLIENT_STATUS}}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="lbl">Failures</div>
      <div class="val">{{TOTAL_FAILURES}} / {{TOTAL_REQUESTS}} <span class="pill {{FAILURE_CLASS}}">{{FAILURE_STATUS}}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="good">
    {{VERDICT_PARAGRAPH}}
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Benchmark Setup</h2>
  <dl class="kv">
    <dt>Connection</dt><dd>{{CONNECTION}}</dd>
    <dt>Database / schema (std)</dt><dd>{{DB_STD}}</dd>
    <dt>Database / schema (int)</dt><dd>{{DB_INT}}</dd>
    <dt>Standard warehouse</dt><dd>{{STD_WH}} · {{STD_WH_DESC}}</dd>
    <dt>Interactive warehouse</dt><dd>{{INT_WH}} · {{INT_WH_DESC}}</dd>
    <dt>Users</dt><dd>{{USER_COUNT}} concurrent (locust <code>--users {{USER_COUNT}} --spawn-rate {{SPAWN_RATE}}</code>)</dd>
    <dt>Duration</dt><dd>{{RUN_TIME}} ({{RUN_TIME_SEC}} s)</dd>
    <dt>Load driver</dt><dd>SPCS BENCHMARK_LOCUST (Locust {{LOCUST_VERSION}}, auto-start / auto-quit)</dd>
    <dt>API layer</dt><dd>SPCS BENCHMARK_API (FastAPI + Snowflake connector) · {{API_WORKERS}} uvicorn workers · POOL_SIZE={{API_POOL_SIZE}} per target · {{API_INSTANCE_FAMILY}} · {{API_INSTANCE_COUNT}} instances</dd>
    <dt>Result caching</dt><dd><code>USE_CACHED_RESULT=FALSE</code> (measures Snowflake, not the result cache)</dd>
    <dt>Query tag</dt><dd><code>QUERY_TAG='IW_BENCHMARK'</code> (used for server-side isolation)</dd>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Query and Filter Variants</h2>
  <p>Locust rotates through the query variants uniformly at random per request, simulating a dashboard where the user changes the date range or applies filters.</p>
  <pre>{{PRIMARY_QUERY}}</pre>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Additional predicate</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{VARIANT_ROWS}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Table Details (Interactive)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Table</th><th class="num">Rows</th><th class="num">Bytes (GB)</th><th>Cluster key</th><th>Aligned with query predicates?</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{TABLE_DETAIL_ROWS}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p style="margin-top:12px">Total working set ≈ <strong>{{WORKING_SET_GB}} GB</strong>. {{WORKING_SET_NOTE}}</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Performance Results — Client-side (Locust HTTP)</h2>
  <p>End-user-observed latency: HTTP round-trip through the SPCS API + Snowflake execution.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th class="num">Requests</th><th class="num">req/s</th><th class="num">Min</th><th class="num">P50</th><th class="num">P90</th><th class="num">P95</th><th class="num">P99</th><th class="num">Max</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{CLIENT_INTERACTIVE_ROW}}
      {{CLIENT_STANDARD_ROW}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p style="margin-top:8px;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px">All values in milliseconds.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Performance Results — Server-side (Snowflake)</h2>
  <p>What Snowflake alone spent — compile + execute + queue — measured from <code>INFORMATION_SCHEMA.QUERY_HISTORY_BY_WAREHOUSE</code> over the run window, filtered to <code>QUERY_TAG='IW_BENCHMARK'</code>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Warehouse</th><th class="num">N</th><th class="num">P50</th><th class="num">P90</th><th class="num">P95</th><th class="num">P99</th><th class="num">Avg compile</th><th class="num">Avg exec</th><th class="num">Avg queue</th><th class="num">Avg MB scan</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{SERVER_INTERACTIVE_ROW}}
      {{SERVER_STANDARD_ROW}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p style="margin-top:8px;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px">All values in milliseconds unless labelled. N is the count of SUCCESS queries observed.</p>
  {{SERVER_N_NOTE}}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Client vs Server — Bottleneck Diagnosis</h2>
  <p>The gap between the client-observed latency (Locust) and the server-side latency (Snowflake) tells us where to optimize.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Percentile</th><th class="num">Locust interactive</th><th class="num">Snowflake interactive</th><th class="num">Δ (API/HTTP/fallback)</th><th class="num">Locust standard</th><th class="num">Snowflake standard</th><th class="num">Δ</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{DELTA_TABLE_ROWS}}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Standard warehouse</h3>
  <p>{{STANDARD_DELTA_ANALYSIS}}</p>

  <h3>Interactive warehouse</h3>
  <p>{{INTERACTIVE_DELTA_ANALYSIS}}</p>

  <div class="{{BOTTLENECK_VERDICT_CLASS}}">
    {{BOTTLENECK_VERDICT}}
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Client-Side Percentile Comparison</h2>
  {{BAR_CLIENT_ROWS}}

  <h3>Server-Side Percentile Comparison (Snowflake alone)</h3>
  {{BAR_SERVER_ROWS}}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Query Profile Health (Interactive, top-slowest)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>QUERY_ID</th><th class="num">Total (ms)</th><th class="num">Compile (ms)</th><th class="num">Execute (ms)</th><th class="num">Queued (ms)</th><th class="num">MB scanned</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{PROFILE_TOP_ROWS}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h3>Verdict</h3>
  <ul>
    {{PROFILE_VERDICT_LIST}}
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Escalation Path</h2>
  <p>Each row is one benchmark iteration. If only one row is present, the target latency was met at the initial configuration and no scale-up or scale-out was required. If multiple rows are present, they show the sequence of Step 13c decisions that led to the reported numbers.</p>
  {{ITERATION_HISTORY}}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Optimization Recommendations</h2>
  <h3>To meet the latency goal</h3>
  {{RECOMMENDATIONS_TO_MEET_GOAL}}

  <h3>Already correct — keep these</h3>
  {{RECOMMENDATIONS_ALREADY_OK}}

  <h3>General guidance for dashboards on Interactive</h3>
  {{RECOMMENDATIONS_GENERAL}}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Configuration Used</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div>
      <h3>Compute pools</h3>
      {{CONFIG_COMPUTE_POOLS}}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>API server (per uvicorn worker)</h3>
      {{CONFIG_API}}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Interactive warehouse</h3>
      {{CONFIG_INT_WH}}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Locust</h3>
      {{CONFIG_LOCUST}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</main>
</body>
</html>
